   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bzs0z1wNiMg9aW37k5wCn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 470,
   "y": 4350,
   "width": 720,
   "height": 850.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "a0052",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1122819322,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 997706677,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1790000000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Not every pass before a shot is a true pass (e.g.\ndefender-to-defender). Score each pass with:\n\n1: Players taken out of the game\nOpponents that were goal-side of the ball before the pass\nand are no longer goal-side of the receiver after it.\nSearch area = half-circle centered on the passer, radius\n= pass length, oriented in pass direction. More players\n-> higher score.\n\n2: Opponents between receiver and goal + shot angle\nCount opponents between receiver and goal before vs after\nthe pass; fewer after -> positive. Shot angle = angle\nbetween the two goal posts seen from the receiver's\nlocation.\n\n3: Progression\nReduction in distance to goal (ball location at pass vs\nat receipt), not only x advance -> wide-to-central passes\nare valued correctly. Balances metrics 1 and 2.\n\n4: Free space around receiver\nCount opponents within radius r = 5 m (start value,\ntunable) of the receiver: in space vs tightly marked.\n\n5: Diagonal passes (modifier, not standalone)\nDiagonal = 20 - 70 deg to the goal axis. Lateral\ndisplacement > 20 m -> flag as switch of play. Changes\nthe weight of the other metrics.\n\nNOTE - candidate metric (to test): goalkeeper position.\nUsed in freeze-frame xG models (keeper distance to goal\nline / to shooter); for passes it may matter only in the\nfinal third.",
   "originalText": "Not every pass before a shot is a true pass (e.g.\ndefender-to-defender). Score each pass with:\n\n1: Players taken out of the game\nOpponents that were goal-side of the ball before the pass\nand are no longer goal-side of the receiver after it.\nSearch area = half-circle centered on the passer, radius\n= pass length, oriented in pass direction. More players\n-> higher score.\n\n2: Opponents between receiver and goal + shot angle\nCount opponents between receiver and goal before vs after\nthe pass; fewer after -> positive. Shot angle = angle\nbetween the two goal posts seen from the receiver's\nlocation.\n\n3: Progression\nReduction in distance to goal (ball location at pass vs\nat receipt), not only x advance -> wide-to-central passes\nare valued correctly. Balances metrics 1 and 2.\n\n4: Free space around receiver\nCount opponents within radius r = 5 m (start value,\ntunable) of the receiver: in space vs tightly marked.\n\n5: Diagonal passes (modifier, not standalone)\nDiagonal = 20 - 70 deg to the goal axis. Lateral\ndisplacement > 20 m -> flag as switch of play. Changes\nthe weight of the other metrics.\n\nNOTE - candidate metric (to test): goalkeeper position.\nUsed in freeze-frame xG models (keeper distance to goal\nline / to shooter); for passes it may matter only in the\nfinal third.",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 8,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
